# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# apps/extension/.env.production
# Copy to `.env.production` in this directory before running `npm run build`.
# Vite reads this automatically for production builds and inlines every
# VITE_-prefixed value directly into the compiled JS bundle (see
# background/api-client.ts's DEFAULT_* constants) - there is no server-side
# step involved on the extension side.
#
# ⚠️  READ THIS BEFORE FILLING IN VALUES BELOW:
# Anything in this file ends up INSIDE the publicly-distributed extension
# (Chrome Web Store packages are just downloadable zips - anyone can unpack
# one and read the JS, minified or not). That means these values are NOT
# secret once you ship a build containing them, in the same sense that a
# browser-exposed Google Maps/Firebase API key isn't secret. That's fine
# here, on purpose - see docs/SECURITY.md "Shared install credentials" for
# the full reasoning - but it does mean:
#   - Do NOT reuse a secret you also use anywhere else.
#   - Treat leakage as inevitable, not as an incident to prevent.
#   - The real defenses against abuse live server-side (per (key+IP) rate
#     limiting, the queue-depth circuit breaker, and the ability to rotate
#     this value + ship a new extension version if it's ever abused) - not
#     the confidentiality of this value.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The one, centrally-hosted server every install of this extension talks to
# by default. Point this at your bought domain once it's live behind Nginx.
VITE_SSENSE_SERVER_URL=https://api.yourdomain.example.com

# Must exactly match one entry in that server's SSENSE_API_KEYS and its
# SSENSE_HMAC_SECRET (see apps/slm-server/.env.example) - generate them
# there first, set them as environment variables ON THE SERVER (never
# committed, never fetched over the network - see DEPLOYMENT.md), and paste
# the SAME values here only for the purpose of baking them into this build.
VITE_SSENSE_API_KEY=
VITE_SSENSE_HMAC_SECRET=
